{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Treat 'move' operations (U1-U6) as relocation of source modules with minimal API adaptation, since the target is the same Spring ecosystem (XD -> Spring Cloud Stream), sharing Spring Integration and Spring Boot foundations.",
    "Treat 'port' operations (U7, U8) as requiring deeper refactoring: processor modules contain more complex business logic (windowing, state, outbound calls) and tighter coupling to XD-specific APIs, so they need closer adaptation to the Spring Cloud Stream binder model.",
    "Group all eight module tasks under a common 'per-module' pattern: (1) copy/relocate Java sources and resources, (2) update package paths and Maven coordinates, (3) adapt to s-c-s Message/Channel APIs and remove XD-specific hooks, (4) port/rewrite unit tests, (5) verify module builds.",
    "Size effort per module primarily by external-protocol/dependency complexity (null < shell < tcp < mqtt < jdbc ≈ splunk < http-client < aggregator) rather than by line count alone.",
    "The s-c-s sink/source contract is fairly thin (MessageHandler / MessageSource with binding via @EnableBinding-equivalent configuration), so a 'move' requires little redesign; only API surface cleanup, package rename, and test verification.",
    "Aggregator and http-client processors are 'ports' because their business logic (window-based aggregation, HTTP invocation) interacts with XD's job/repository/launcher abstractions that do not exist in s-c-s and must be replaced by s-c-s-friendly equivalents (e.g., in-memory state vs. XD JobRepository; RestTemplate/WebClient vs. XD's HttpClientFactory).",
    "Common cross-cutting work (repo module structure, parent POM updates, integration testing harness, documentation) is broken out as separate activities rather than baked into each module.",
    "All estimates assume the developer is experienced with Spring Integration, Spring Cloud Stream, Maven, and the existing Spring XD codebase; estimates would be substantially higher for a novice."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Each module's source code in Spring XD is well-structured, has unit tests, and uses standard Spring APIs (Spring Integration, JDBC, MQTT client, etc.) so relocation is mechanical rather than redesign.",
    "The s-c-s target repository already exists with proper module layout; this increment only adds the eight modules, not the surrounding infrastructure.",
    "Dependency upgrades (Spring Boot, Spring Integration, Spring Cloud Stream versions) are not part of this increment; the modules are migrated against an existing s-c-s baseline.",
    "No new features or behavior changes are introduced; the goal is functional equivalence of the modules in the new repository.",
    "Integration testing uses embedded/test binder and in-memory message channels rather than real external systems (no live MQTT broker, Splunk instance, JDBC database, shell host, TCP peer, or HTTP server are required).",
    "Functional/regression testing against live external systems is out of scope and handled by the receiving team or follow-up tickets.",
    "One developer performs all activities sequentially; no parallelization is assumed in the effort total.",
    "Code review is not separately estimated and is folded into the per-module activities as part of polishing/refactoring."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project setup and module skeleton in s-c-s repo",
      "activity_description": "Create Maven module directories for the eight new modules in the s-c-s repository, add entries to the parent POM, configure shared dependencies (Spring Integration, Spring Cloud Stream binder test support), and verify the multi-module build compiles before any module code is added."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Move mqtt sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the XD mqtt sink sources, rename packages, adapt to s-c-s MessageHandler contract, port unit tests using an embedded MQTT broker or test binder, and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Move null sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the trivial 'null' sink (no-op MessageHandler), rename packages, ensure the module is registered as a s-c-s sink option, add/update a minimal unit test, and verify build."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Move shell sink module (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the XD shell sink that executes a shell command per payload, adapt to s-c-s MessageHandler, remove XD-specific process-launching hooks, port unit tests, and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Move splunk sink module (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the XD splunk HTTP Event Collector sink, adapt to s-c-s MessageHandler, update Splunk HEC client dependency and configuration properties, port unit tests (likely using a mock HTTP server), and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Move tcp sink module (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the XD tcp sink (server socket listening on a port), adapt to s-c-s MessageHandler, ensure lifecycle (open/close) and inbound payload handling are correct in s-c-s, port unit tests, and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Move jdbc source module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the XD jdbc source (polling MessageSource from a SQL query), adapt to s-c-s MessageSource contract, ensure transaction/poll lifecycle is preserved, port unit tests (likely with an embedded H2 or HSQLDB), and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Port aggregator processor module (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD aggregator module to a s-c-s processor. Replace XD JobRepository/launcher-based state management with in-memory state appropriate for s-c-s, adapt aggregation/windowing logic to the s-c-s Message/Channel API, port and adjust unit tests, and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Port http-client processor module (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD http-client processor to a s-c-s processor. Replace XD's HttpClientFactory with Spring's RestTemplate/WebClient, adapt request/response mapping to s-c-s Message types, port unit tests (using MockWebServer or MockRestServiceServer), and verify the module builds and tests pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing of all migrated modules",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end integration tests that wire each migrated module (mqtt, null, shell, splunk, tcp, jdbc, aggregator, http-client) into a s-c-s stream definition using the test binder, verify messages flow correctly, fix any cross-module interaction issues, and ensure the full multi-module build (including the eight new modules) is green."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and migration notes",
      "activity_description": "Add per-module README sections describing the sink/source/processor options and their configuration properties in s-c-s, update the top-level s-c-s docs to list the newly moved/ported modules, and write a short migration note describing differences from the XD originals."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 71
  }
}
```

